<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jadwiga of Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Queen Jadwiga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jadwiga was crowned ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in the late fourteenth century. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-krewo">Union of Krewo</a> of 1385 she married the Lithuanian grand duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a>, who accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and became King Władysław II Jagiełło. Their marriage began the dynastic union of Poland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jadwiga-of-poland.jpg" alt="Jadwiga of Poland" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jadwiga_Andegawe%C5%84ska_seal_1386.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
